  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared per RBC-RAD-07. Four booked studies; three cancelled appointments skipped (appt-00001, -00006, -00008).\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0001). No contrast allergy. T2DM, diet only. Last creatinine (9/24) was outside the 30-day window, so a pre-scan creatinine was ordered (sr-t0009). Late result: outside creatinine 1.52 on 10/22. Not AKI by policy criteria (28 days from the 0.94 baseline), eGFR about 64, so no change to prep. Rise flagged to Dr. Okafor (task-t0030). Instructions sent (comm-t0012).\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0002). Allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\", but the 2019 radiology report grades the reaction moderate. Premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 10/25 20:00, 10/26 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0005); diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0006); driver needed. Late correction: the 10/14 creatinine is really 2.8 (eGFR about 24). The 0.98 first reported was another patient's sample. Added NS 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0019) and sent corrected Spanish/English instructions to arrive by 08:00 (comm-t0023). Workup task for Dr. Okafor (task-t0029).\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0003). AKI at the ED 10/4-10/5 with no follow-up creatinine since. Ordered a pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0010) and NS 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0007). Metformin (mr-00392) on hold, last dose 10/25 evening. Task at 48 h after the scan to recheck creatinine and restart metformin only if kidney function is normal (task-t0011). Late outside report: moderate iopamidol reaction in 2022. Added prednisone 50 mg at 10/26 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0020) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0021). Updated instructions sent (comm-t0024). Iopamidol could not be coded from the formulary, so a task to add the allergy to the list was created (task-t0031).\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004). No prep needed; patient told (comm-t0015). Late outside report of a mild iohexol reaction in 2024 was recorded as an allergy (alg-t0022); no effect on this non-contrast scan.\n\nNotes and addenda documenting each decision are signed. The four new inbox items were reviewed and completed. Older inbox items unrelated to this task were left untouched.",
